{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And HaShem set a time, saying.</b> That is, He informed them of the time of the plague, so that they would bring their livestock in from the fields — as we find that He did with the plague of hail, where HaShem stated the matter explicitly, as it is written (Exodus 9:19): ״שְׁלַח הָעֵז״ and so forth. But here He stated the matter by allusion, and this is what He intended by the word <b>לֵאמֹר</b> — meaning, that Moses and Aaron would communicate the setting of this appointed time to Pharaoh and to the Egyptians, for this is the intended purpose, as we have explained."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:59.007724800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}